        <div class="mo-fit__col mo-fit__col--out">
          <h3 class="ac-type-h3-home-route">Probably not a fit</h3>
          <ul class="mo-minus-list">
            {poorFit.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
          </ul>
          <p class="mo-fit__aside">
            If the property still holds too much to reach the surfaces, clearing has to happen
            before cleaning can start — see <a href="/property-cleanouts-san-jose/">property
            cleanouts</a>. If the main issue is a family estate transition rather than a
            straightforward move-out, <a href="/estate-cleanout-san-jose/">estate cleanout</a> may
            fit better. If there is no handoff deadline and you just want a detailed one-time
            clean, see <a href="/deep-cleaning-san-jose/">detailed deep cleaning</a>. Not sure?
            Send photos. We will say whether it sounds like a fit.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mo-price">
        <div class="mo-price__copy">
          <h3 class="ac-type-h3-home-feature">Size tells us how much property there is. Condition tells us how much work it needs.</h3>
          <p>
            A vacant two-bedroom in good shape and an occupied four-bedroom with heavy kitchen
            buildup are not the same job at the same size. Occupancy status, condition, and how
            much detail you want all move the price.
          </p>
          <p class="mo-price__fee">{site.offer.assessmentFraming(site.offer.assessmentFee)}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mo-price__drivers">
          <p class="mo-price__label">What moves the number</p>
          <ul class="mo-rule-list mo-rule-list--tight">
            {priceDrivers.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ══ 07 · QUESTIONS ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
